---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="NO BALL GAMES Collections | Original Art, Painted Clothing, Digital Collectibles &amp; XRP KIDs"
  description="Collect the NO BALL GAMES story: original Grime Art paintings, hand-painted wearables, digital collectibles and the XRP KIDs lore universe."
  current="collections"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">Collections</span>
    <h1>Collect the story — physical and digital.</h1>
    <p>
      NO BALL GAMES spans original Grime Art paintings, hand-painted wearable clothing, digital collectibles and the XRP KIDs lore universe. Every piece carries the mark of street culture: raw, British, one-of-one.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>Collector categories</h2>
      <p>Four lanes. All grounded in the same Grime Art energy and sign-flip identity.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card-grid">
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Original art</span>
        <h3>One-of-one Grime Art paintings</h3>
        <p>Original one-of-one artworks: sign-flip canvases, pop-culture portrait pieces, mixed-media experiments and raw studio output shaped by Charlie Buster's Grime Art visual language. Premium originals with provenance, story and the mark of a human hand.</p>
        <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}contact/`}>Enquire about originals →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Painted clothing</span>
        <h3>Wearable Grime Art pieces</h3>
        <p>Custom painted military jackets, denim and wearable art produced as collectible pieces. Each jacket is a canvas in its own right: graffiti texture, Grime Art energy and one-of-one finish on a real garment base. Commissions are open.</p>
        <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}contact/`}>Order painted clothing →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Prints and editions</span>
        <h3>Signed prints and edition runs</h3>
        <p>Signed print releases and controlled edition drops for collectors who want entry points into the Grime Art world while retaining premium presentation and story context.</p>
        <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}contact/`}>Ask about editions →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">Digital collectibles</span>
        <h3>Lore-linked digital objects</h3>
        <p>Digital collectible concepts, character drops, collector passes and lore-connected releases tied to the NO BALL GAMES universe. Digital collectibles carry the same cultural weight as physical work — story, scarcity and brand identity baked in from the start.</p>
        <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}xrp/`}>Explore XRP KIDs universe →</a>
      </article>
      <article class="feature-card">
        <span class="kicker">XRP KIDs</span>
        <h3>100 genesis KIDs — 89 captured, 11 free</h3>
        <p>XRP KIDs is the XRP-side NO BALL GAMES lore branch: 100 genesis KIDs, Alpha Aaron's machine capture arc, FRET's resistance network, the $PMSL hard-fork shield and Block Buster OG lore objects. The XRP KIDs universe is the digital collectible home of the NO BALL GAMES story.</p>
        <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}xrp/`}>Enter the XRP KIDs universe →</a>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section split-grid">
    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">Physical collector lane</span>
      <h2>Original art and wearables.</h2>
      <ul class="list-clean">
        <li>Original one-of-one artworks with medium, size and provenance detail.</li>
        <li>Custom painted military jackets, denim and wearable art with garment base and finish notes.</li>
        <li>Signed prints and edition releases for broader collector access.</li>
        <li>Commissioned pieces via direct enquiry — describe your vision, Charlie Buster makes it.</li>
        <li>Limited physical drops announced through community channels.</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}contact/`}>Commission a piece →</a>
    </article>

    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">Digital collector lane</span>
      <h2>XRP KIDs and digital drops.</h2>
      <ul class="list-clean">
        <li>XRP KIDs universe collectibles linked to the NO BALL GAMES lore arc.</li>
        <li>Character drops, faction pieces and lore-edition releases.</li>
        <li>Block Buster OG and $PMSL-connected lore objects in collector storytelling.</li>
        <li>Community participation through FRET and the resistance arc.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="coming-soon-tag">Always verify issuer, collection and marketplace before interacting with any digital asset. Not financial advice.</div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section cta-block">
    <div class="cta-block-inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">Ready to collect?</span>
      <h2>Commission art. Order clothing. Explore XRP KIDs.</h2>
      <p>All collector enquiries — originals, painted jackets, digital collectibles and XRP KIDs — go through contact.</p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="button primary" href={`${base}contact/`}>Start your enquiry</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href={`${base}xrp/`}>Explore XRP KIDs</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
